    "reason": "The English lemma 'position' is a broad noun with multiple meanings (e.g., physical location, job, stance/opinion). The Japanese expression '旗幟' (きし) primarily means 'flag/banner' and secondarily refers to 'one's stance/position/opinion' (as per JMdict Sense 1). This makes it semantically 'NARROW' as it only covers one specific, abstract sense of 'position'. Furthermore, '旗幟' is a formal and somewhat literary word, not a natural or common term a general language learner would expect for 'position' in daily life, especially given the 'general, daily_life' domain. More common and natural alternatives exist for the 'stance/opinion' sense.",
